# File: scripts/__tests__/sdlc-worktree.test.mjs, scripts/__tests__/sdlc-merge-queue.test.mjs, scripts/__tests__/sdlc-verification-runtime.test.mjs, scripts/__tests__/sdlc-finalize-verification.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/551-add-parallel-delivery-with-worktree-isolation-a-merge-queue-change-scoped-validation-tiers-and-one-pass-verification/requirements.md
Feature: Parallel delivery with worktrees, a merge queue, validation tiers and one-pass verification

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Concurrent runs use separate worktrees and leave the primary checkout untouched
    Given a primary checkout on the default branch with uncommitted changes
    When two execute runs for different issues and one spec publication start at the same time
    Then each run uses its own worktree under the sibling worktree root created from the remote default branch
    And no run reports default_checkout_failed, issue_branch_unreadable or branch_checkout_failed
    And the primary checkout's branch, HEAD and status are unchanged

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Spec and code branches never collide
    Given issue N has an open code PR on branch "{N}-{slug}"
    When the spec for N is published
    Then publication uses branch "spec/{N}-{slug}" and never merges the code PR

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Queue head integrates alone and validates once
    Given branches A and B passed review and entered the merge queue in that order
    When the queue processes them
    Then B starts no pre-merge validation until A has merged
    And each branch runs its pre-merge validations exactly once after merging the default branch

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Queued branches never share a version or conflict on the changelog
    Given a project opted into changelog fragments and two queued branches with fragments
    When both merge through the queue
    Then the merges produce different versions, both fragments are assembled into CHANGELOG.md, and no integration conflicts

  @SCN005
  Scenario: A failing queue head leaves the queue
    Given a queue head whose pre-merge validations fail after integrating the default branch
    When the failure is recorded
    Then the branch leaves the queue with reason "queue_gate_failed", its version commit is reverted, and it returns to implement
    And the next queue entry proceeds

  @SCN006
  Scenario: Overlapping in-flight issues are reported at start
    Given an in-flight issue M whose spec declares a file that issue N's spec also declares
    When the controller starts issue N
    Then the start stage report lists issue M and the overlapping files

  @SCN007
  Scenario: Heavy jobs share a host-wide pool
    Given heavyJobSlots is 1 and two processes start heavy validations
    When both start
    Then the validations run one after the other, the second records its wait, and a dead holder's slot is reclaimed

  @SCN008
  Scenario: Status shows queue and pool state
    Given in-flight worktrees, queued branches and heavy-job slot holders
    When status runs with --json
    Then the parallel object lists in-flight issues with stage and queue position, the queue, the slot holders and leftover worktrees

  @SCN009
  Scenario: Change tier runs selected tests outside fallback paths
    Given a change-tier validation with a selection provider and fallback paths
    When a change touches only non-fallback files and the provider returns a fresh selection
    Then the selected tests run and the record shows tier, provider, reason "selected", count and data age

  @SCN010
  Scenario: Fallback paths and stale selection data run the full command
    Given a change-tier validation with a selection provider and fallback paths
    When a change touches a fallback path or the provider reports missing or stale data
    Then the full command runs and the record states the fallback reason

  @SCN011
  Scenario: Full tier runs on demand and reports regressions
    Given a full-tier validation
    When /sdlc-verify-full runs against a ref and fails
    Then the result is recorded for that commit and the commits since the last green full record are listed

  @SCN012
  Scenario: Downstream actions can require a full-green commit
    Given steering declares the full-green action "deploy"
    When the check runs for a commit
    Then it answers green only when a passed full record exists at or after that commit

  @SCN013
  Scenario: Projects without tiers keep today's behaviour
    Given validations that declare no tier
    When the pre-merge gate runs
    Then every required validation runs its full command and records no tier or selection

  @SCN014
  Scenario: One verify pass reports every finding without running validations
    Given a change with two independent blocking defects
    When verify runs once
    Then one failed handoff reports both findings and no pre-merge validation runs

  @SCN015
  Scenario: Unevaluated checklist rows block the handoff
    Given a review checklist with a row that has no verdict
    When the finalizer receives the review
    Then it refuses with "review_checklist_incomplete" and names the unevaluated rows

  @SCN016
  Scenario: Repair re-verification is scoped
    Given a prior review with findings and a repair commit
    When verify runs after the repair
    Then the scope is "scoped" when the repair stays within the findings' files and "full" naming outside paths otherwise
